cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it using the following metadata."
title: "Explainable Hybrid Deep Learning-Based Network Intrusion Detection System"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-16"
url: "https://github.com/norriy0u/Explainable-Hybrid-Deep-Learning-IDS"
repository-code: "https://github.com/norriy0u/Explainable-Hybrid-Deep-Learning-IDS"
license: MIT
abstract: >
  An intelligent, explainable network intrusion detection system (IDS) that combines
  one-dimensional convolutional neural networks (1D-CNN), Bidirectional Long Short-Term Memory
  (BiLSTM) networks, trainable temporal attention mechanisms, and SHAP (SHapley Additive
  exPlanations) to classify network traffic into ten categories on the UNSW-NB15 benchmark dataset.
  The system provides a full Streamlit SOC dashboard for interactive detection, model training,
  and explainability analysis.
keywords:
  - intrusion detection
  - cybersecurity
  - deep learning
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - CNN
  - BiLSTM
  - attention mechanism
  - network security
  - UNSW-NB15
  - PyTorch
  - Keras
  - Streamlit
